From 7c9b00a1807317ae47c35440b960a71bd2190286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EssenMoon <yueqrgg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:20:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix UltiSnips + Auto Pairs example to keep snippets in
 Insert mode

The UltiSnips + Auto Pairs example chained <plug>AutoPairsReturn after
<plug>UltiExpand:

    imap <plug>MyCR <plug>UltiExpand<plug>AutoPairsReturn
    imap <cr> <plug>MyCR

That makes <plug>AutoPairsReturn run unconditionally, including right
after a snippet has been expanded.  Its <esc>-based return handling can
then leave Insert mode, breaking the just-expanded snippet: the jump
trigger no longer moves between the snippet's placeholders.

Put the fallback keys inside the argument to
mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet() instead, so they are used only
when no pop-up menu is visible:

    inoremap <silent> <expr> <plug>UltiExpand
          \ mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet(
          \     "<cr><plug>AutoPairsReturn")
    imap <cr> <plug>UltiExpand

Also document why chaining the fallback in a recursive imap leads to
E223: Recursive mapping.
---
 doc/mucomplete.txt | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/mucomplete.txt b/doc/mucomplete.txt
index d6b195c..30ed3c3 100644
--- a/doc/mucomplete.txt
+++ b/doc/mucomplete.txt
@@ -1232,7 +1232,10 @@ You still need to redefine UltiSnips's mappings as explained above.
 UltiSnips + Auto Pairs ~
 If you want snippets to be expanded as explained above and you are using Auto
 Pairs, you need to disable Auto Pairs's mappings and invoke them in custom
-mappings, as follows:
+mappings.  Put the fallback keys (here, a plain <cr> followed by
+<plug>AutoPairsReturn) *inside* the argument to
+mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet() rather than chaining them after
+<plug>UltiExpand:
 >
 	let g:AutoPairsMapCR = 0
 	let g:AutoPairsMapSpace = 0
@@ -1241,10 +1244,26 @@ mappings, as follows:
 	  \ : "<c-r>=AutoPairsSpace()<cr>"
 
 	inoremap <silent> <expr> <plug>UltiExpand
-	      \ mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet("\<cr>")
+	      \ mucomplete#ultisnips#expand_snippet(
+	      \     "\<cr>\<plug>AutoPairsReturn")
+	imap <cr> <plug>UltiExpand
+<
+This way Auto Pairs' <plug>AutoPairsReturn runs only when no pop-up menu is
+visible.  If it is chained *after* <plug>UltiExpand, as in:
+>
 	imap <plug>MyCR <plug>UltiExpand<plug>AutoPairsReturn
 	imap <cr> <plug>MyCR
 <
+then <plug>AutoPairsReturn also runs right after a snippet has been expanded.
+Its <esc>-based handling may then leave Insert mode, which breaks the
+just-expanded snippet (you can no longer jump between its placeholders with
+the jump trigger).
+<
+Note also that a plain <cr> inside the fallback argument is returned directly
+by the expression mapping, so it does not go through the <cr> mapping again;
+putting the fallback in a recursive `imap` chain that expands to another
+<cr> would cause an `E223: Recursive mapping` error.
+<
 UltiSnips + PHP ~
